  "term": "BOLD",
  "definition": "BOLD is a functional MRI method that estimates brain activity by detecting differences in the MRI signal between oxygen-rich and oxygen-poor hemoglobin. Because these signal changes reflect metabolic activity, it is used to infer neurologic activity in the brain.",
